# CLAUDE.md

Per-repo orientation for `${git_provider.org}/${project_name}` — ArgoCD-managed
Kubernetes manifests for the homelab cluster.

## Homelab universals

- **Toolchain pinned via `mise.toml`**; task runner `just` (positional dispatch).
- **`.env` is a [1Password Developer Environment](https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/local-env-file)** file. `op run --env-file=.env -- <cmd>`. Never `source .env`.
- **`OnePasswordItem` CRs** reference items via `vaults/<id>/items/<id>`.
- **`docz create <type> "Title"`** for ADR / RFC / DESIGN / IMPL / INV.
- **Trunk-based for Argo work**: commit straight to `main` — PR review delays sync.
- **Capture cross-cutting surprises in the active IMPL's Follow-Ups**; no silent workarounds.
- **`grep` is `rg`** — regex is the default. Drop `-E`.
- **Verify CRD schema, don't grep rendered YAML** — `kubectl explain <crd>.spec --recursive`.
- **Alpha-API debug**: when one schema error reveals the next, dump the full schema.

## Repo layout

```
apps/<group>/<app>/              # per-app kustomize + helmCharts
apps/<group>/application-set.yaml
infra/<group>/<app>/             # cluster-level infrastructure
```

ArgoCD watches `${git_provider.org}/${project_name}` and syncs everything under
`apps/*` + `infra/*` to the homelab cluster.

## Deployment conventions

- **Kustomize `helmCharts` (not raw helm)** for chart-based deploys.
  Chart pinning in `kustomization.yaml`; overrides in `values.yaml`.
- **OCI chart URLs**: `oci://ghcr.io/org/charts` (kustomize appends the
  chart name — do NOT include it in the repo field).
- **ApplicationSets**: Go-template (`goTemplate: true`) with
  `.path.basename` (dot prefix). New AppSets MUST use goTemplate.
- **Gateway API**: HTTPRoute for HTTP, GRPCRoute for gRPC. TCPRoute is
  NOT supported by Cilium — use a LoadBalancer Service with BGP labels.
- **`GrafanaDashboard` CRs**: custom dashboards follow the alloy-external
  pattern. JSON in `data/<name>.json` next to the manifest;
  `configMapGenerator` with `disableNameSuffixHash: true` bakes it into
  a ConfigMap; the CR references via `configMapRef`. Cross-namespace
  pickup is on (`allowCrossNamespaceImport: true`,
  `instanceSelector: app=grafana`).
- **Image pinning + Renovate**: every chart bump pins the app image
  explicitly in `values.yaml` (or the resource CR for non-chart deploys)
  with `# renovate: image=<repo>` one line above the tag. Chart-version
  bump and image-pin land as separate commits.
- **Pre-flight snapshots**: before any IMPL phase that touches CRDs or
  shared cluster state, snapshot affected resources to
  `docs/impl/snapshots/<impl>-<date>-<scope>.yaml` (use
  `kubectl get … -o yaml --show-managed-fields=false`).

## Storage gotchas

- **RWO PVC + single-replica Deployment**: default `strategy: Recreate`,
  not RollingUpdate. RollingUpdate deadlocks because the new pod can't
  attach the volume while the old one still holds it.
- **ext4 `emergency_ro` on democratic-csi iSCSI**: a single failed write
  (TrueNAS blip, controller reset) can trigger `JBD2: I/O error` →
  ext4 `errors=remount-ro` flips the FS read-only. Pod keeps running
  on cached RW state until a scheduled write surfaces it
  (`IOException: Read-only file system`). Diagnose via `/proc/mounts`
  containing `emergency_ro`. **Recovery**: pause ArgoCD auto-sync →
  `kubectl scale --replicas=0` (CSI logs out iSCSI session) → scale back
  to 1 (kernel runs journal recovery on re-stage) → restore auto-sync.
  Writes since the original event are lost.
- **Pause/unpause sync without an AppSet revert**: AppSet template
  overrides direct App patches. Patch the AppSet, not the App, when
  you need a transient `syncPolicy: automated: null`.

## CNPG (Postgres) gotchas

- **Inline `spec.backup.barmanObjectStore` is deprecated in 1.27, REMOVED
  in 1.28**. Migration target: `plugin-barman-cloud` chart. Per-cluster,
  atomic single-commit: drop `spec.backup.*`, add a `spec.plugins[]`
  entry referencing an `ObjectStore` CR. Triggers a rolling restart.
- **Path-style S3 (Garage/MinIO) is NOT a boto3 env var**. The actual
  knob is `--addressing-style=path` plumbed through
  `data.additionalCommandArgs` / `wal.archiveAdditionalCommandArgs` /
  `wal.restoreAdditionalCommandArgs` on the `ObjectStore` CR (asymmetric
  field names per sub-block). Works because the plugin sidecar bundles
  barman 3.18.0+. Garage also needs
  `AWS_REQUEST_CHECKSUM_CALCULATION=when_required` +
  `AWS_RESPONSE_CHECKSUM_VALIDATION=when_required` on
  `instanceSidecarConfiguration.env`.
- **`ensure_sufficient_disk_space` guard**: when PVCs hit ~100% the
  operator blocks ALL reconciliation including its own PVC expansion.
  `cnpg.io/hibernation: "on"` won't help — the guard runs first.
  Recovery: bypass operator, patch PVCs directly via `kubectl patch
  pvc` (volume expansion via CSI), `kubectl delete pod` to force FS
  resize on next mount.
- **CNPG `Pooler` + ArgoCD flapping** is expected — selfHeal reapplies
  Pooler CR, CNPG recreates child resources. Don't chase.

## Monitoring gotchas

- **`kube-prometheus-stack` CRD upgrades** need
  `kubectl apply --server-side --force-conflicts` because Helm previously
  owned the field manager on those CRDs. Plain `kubectl apply` fails
  with field-manager conflicts. Skip intermediate operator versions —
  CRDs are forward-compatible, apply only the target version.
- **Grafana 13+ rejects default `[rendering]renderer_token`** in
  production — pod CrashLoopBackOff. Set a non-default token on BOTH
  the Grafana CR (`spec.config.rendering.renderer_token`) AND the
  `grafana-image-renderer` Deployment (`AUTH_TOKEN` env).
- **`alloy` DaemonSet has no positions persistence**. The chart mounts
  only the config configmap, no `/var/lib/alloy` hostPath. Every alloy
  pod restart re-reads logs from the kubelet API; Loki rejects entries
  older than `reject_old_samples_max_age` (168h). Visible as transient
  dropped-entry flood; drains in 2–5 min. Fix is hostPath for
  `/var/lib/alloy`.
- **Atlantis exports Prometheus summaries, not histograms** — quantile
  buckets return `NaN` at low volume. Use
  `rate(metric_sum[5m]) / rate(metric_count[5m])` for avg-duration panels.

## Atlantis (deployed here, owned by tf-live) gotchas

- **Init container needs `securityContext.runAsUser: 0`** — StatefulSet
  sets `runAsUser: 100`, blocks `apk add`.
- **`ATLANTIS_WRITE_GIT_CREDS`** is auto-injected when `githubApp` is set;
  don't also set it in `environment` block (ServerSideApply rejects).
- **`vcsSecretName`** uses a single secret for both `key.pem` (volume
  mount) AND `github_secret` (env var) — can't split across two secrets.
- **GitHub App `events: []` silent drop**: webhooks arrive with 200 OK
  but never trigger autoplan unless the App is subscribed to
  `pull_request` / `issue_comment` / `pull_request_review` / `push`.
  UI-only at `https://github.com/settings/apps/<slug>` → Permissions &
  events. Cannot be set via the API.
- **chart `githubApp.id`** must be quoted string (`"3354082"`) to avoid
  scientific-notation rendering.

## OTel / span_metrics gotchas

- **Langfuse 3.172+ emits OTel TRACES only, NOT metrics**. For RED
  dashboards, use the otel-collector's `span_metrics` connector to
  synthesize rate/error/duration from the trace stream.
- **`span_metrics` traps**: `service.name` is a built-in dimension —
  listing it explicitly under `dimensions` fails validation.
  `resource_to_telemetry_conversion: true` on the prometheus exporter
  is a cardinality bomb. Always filter `kind == Server` before
  span_metrics, otherwise outbound HTTP client spans (URL paths with
  UUIDs) explode series count. If the collector forwards traces to the
  service that produced them, filter `resource.service.name` BEFORE
  tail_sampling to break the feedback loop.

## ClickHouse (langfuse namespace) gotchas

- **ClickHouse Inc. operator chart `clickhouse-operator-helm`** ships a
  `v1alpha1` CRD set NOT API-compatible with the Altinity
  `ClickHouseInstallation` shape. Key traps for `ClickHouseCluster`:
  - Group is `clickhouse.com`, not `clickhouse.altinity.com`.
  - `defaultUserPassword`, `extraConfig`, `extraUsersConfig`, `logger`,
    `tls` nest under `spec.settings`, NOT at `spec` top level.
  - `containerTemplate.image` is structured
    `{repository, tag, hash}`, not a string. NO `name` field — it's a
    singular spec, not a container list.
  - `podTemplate` has NO `containers:` slot, only `initContainers`.
    Sidecars (e.g. clickhouse-backup) run as standalone Deployments.
  - Verify with `kubectl explain chc.spec --recursive`, not chart YAML.

## Other recurring gotchas

- **ArgoCD repo-server connection drops** periodically — restart
  application controller + repo-server.
- **Technitium DNS blocks cert-manager ACME DNS-01** — set
  `--dns01-recursive-nameservers=1.1.1.1:53` +
  `--dns01-recursive-nameservers-only=true` in cert-manager args.
- **MySQL Docker image only runs init on empty data dir** — password
  rotations without PVC reset → credentials mismatch.
- **Forgejo runner chart (wrenix)** is unmaintained — set
  `knownLastVersion: true` in chart values.

